    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/dom/issues/141",
    "id": 168753410,
    "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE2ODc1MzQxMA==",
    "user": {
      "login": "bzbarsky",
      "id": 1457979,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0NTc5Nzk=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1457979?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bzbarsky",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2016-01-04T18:02:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-04T18:02:48Z",
    "body": "The list should in theory include all names which return something other than `undefined` for `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor`, right?\n\nThis actually kinda sucks; due to the lowercasing behavior this means that all possible uppercasings should be in the list, or something.  That seems fairly undesirable, not to mention probably not so web-compatible.\n\nNow the good news is that since named props can't be made non-configurable and objects with such props can't be made non-extensible there isn't actually a violation of the spec section you cite here if we just have `[[OwnPropertyKeys]]` return some subset of the things that will return useful stuff from `[[GetOwnProperty]]`.  It's slightly weird behavior, but not inherently contradicting the ES spec.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
